.\" quasselcore-rs.1 -- the Quassel core, in Rust
.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt QUASSELCORE-RS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm quasselcore-rs
.Nd the Quassel IRC core, in Rust
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -c Ar path
.Op Fl -p Ar port
.Op Fl -listen Ar address
.Nm
.Fl -add-user
.Nm
.Fl -change-userpass Ar username
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the daemon of Quassel IRC.
It holds the IRC connections and the chat history; the clients connect to it
and talk the Quassel protocol to it.
Because the state lives in the core, a client can be closed and opened again
without losing anything, and several clients can watch the same conversation.
.Pp
The core speaks the same protocol as the C++ core, so the existing clients
work with it, and it reads and writes the same databases.
.Pp
The options are listed in
.Sx OPTIONS .
The configuration file,
.Pa quasselcore.conf ,
is described in
.Sx CONFIGURATION .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -c Ar path , Fl -configdir Ar path
The directory that holds the configuration file, the database and the
certificate.
The default is
.Pa $HOME/.config/quassel.org/quasselcore .
.It Fl -listen Ar address
The addresses the core listens on.
Several addresses are separated by commas.
The default is
.Ql ::,0.0.0.0 ,
which is every address of both families.
.It Fl -p Ar port , Fl -port Ar port
The port the core listens at.
The default is 4242.
.It Fl -n , Fl -norestore
This option is reserved.
The core does not restore the state of the last run yet, and it says so when
the option is used.
.It Fl -select-backend Ar name
The storage backend to use for this run:
.Cm SQLite
or
.Cm PostgreSQL .
The data is not migrated: a database of the other backend is not touched.
.It Fl -select-authenticator Ar id
The authenticator to use.
The only one there is at the moment is
.Cm Database ;
any other value is refused.
.It Fl -add-user
Add a user.
The user name and the password are asked for on the terminal.
.It Fl -change-userpass Ar username
Change the password of a user.
.It Fl -user Ar name
The user name for
.Fl -add-user .
The user whose password is changed is the one of
.Fl -change-userpass ;
the two options cannot be used together.
The name is not a secret.
.It Fl -password-file Ar path
Read the password from this file instead of asking for it.
The file holds the password on its first line.
The password is never taken from the command line, where any other process
could read it out of the process list.
.It Fl -require-tls , Fl -require-ssl
Refuse the clients that do not use TLS.
.It Fl -tls-cert Ar path , Fl -ssl-cert Ar path
The certificate the core serves.
The default is
.Pa quasselCert.pem
in the configuration directory.
.It Fl -tls-key Ar path , Fl -ssl-key Ar path
The private key of the certificate.
The default is the certificate file itself.
.It Fl -strict-ident
This option is reserved.
The core does not answer ident requests yet, and it refuses the option.
.It Fl -L Ar level , Fl -loglevel Ar level
The log level:
.Cm Debug ,
.Cm Info ,
.Cm Warning
or
.Cm Error .
The default is
.Cm Info .
.It Fl -l Ar path , Fl -logfile Ar path
Log to this file as well as to the standard error.
.It Fl -d , Fl -debug
Log at the debug level.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The core reads
.Pa quasselcore.conf
from its configuration directory.
The file is in the INI format that Qt's
.Ql QSettings
writes; a key of a sub-group is written with a backslash.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[Core]
StorageSettings\eBackend=SQLite
StorageSettings\eConnectionProperties\eDatabase=quassel-storage.sqlite
AuthSettings\eAuthenticator=Database

[Core\eSSL]
Certificate=/var/db/quasselcore/quasselCert.pem
Key=/var/db/quasselcore/quasselCert.pem
SystemCA=true
.Ed
.Pp
The storage backend is either
.Cm SQLite ,
a file in the configuration directory, or
.Cm PostgreSQL ,
whose connection properties are in the file under
.Ql StorageSettings\eConnectionProperties .
.Pp
The certificate is one PEM file that holds the private key and the
certificate, concatenated.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa quasselcore.conf
The configuration of the core, in the configuration directory.
.It Pa quassel-storage.sqlite
The SQLite database, in the configuration directory.
.It Pa quasselCert.pem
The certificate and the private key, in the configuration directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Nm quassel ,
the graphical client.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The Quassel project ,
and the authors of the Rust port.
.Sh BUGS
Report the bugs to the issue tracker of the repository.
